      "math_academy_id": "q-76641",
      "knowledge_point_id": "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula",
      "problem": "Find the exact value of $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$",
